          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'assemble 8 full sequences (K-Q-J...A) of the SAME SUIT.',
          gameplay: 'Build down by rank on the tableau (any suit); in-suit sequences may be moved together. A complete run of 13 cards in one suit (King down to Ace) is removed from the tableau. When no column is empty, deal 10 cards from the stock (one per column). Continue until all eight sequences are removed (win) or no legal move and no deal remains (loss).',
          keyRules: [
            'Tableau builds down by rank; any suit.',
            'In-suit sequences may be moved as a unit.',
            'Complete K-to-A same suit is removed from play.',
            'Deal 10 from stock only when no column is empty.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Prioritize emptying piles to turn over face-down cards. An empty pile is goldâ€”it lets you move any junk card there to unblock others. In 2/4 Suit, try to keep piles 'pure' (same suit) as much as possible so you can move them later.",
          intermediate: "The 'Tidy Up' Phase: Before dealing a new row, tidy up your runs. Make sure sequences are as consolidated as possible. If you have a choice between putting a 5-Hearts on a 6-Hearts or 6-Spades, choose Hearts.",
          advanced: 'Sacrificing a Run: Sometimes playing a 5-Hearts on a 6-Spades (blocking the run) is necessary to uncover a face-down card that might be a King. Uncovering cards > Maintaining runs.',
          tips: [
            "Don't fill an empty space with a King unless necessary.",
            'Undo is your friend in 4-Suit.',
          ],
